+# Summary
+
+**Changed:** implemented `satisfies()` and `max_satisfying()` in `depres/ranges.py` per `docs/RANGES.md` (comparator sets with `||`, primitive operators, partials/X-ranges, hyphen, tilde, caret, prerelease rule, `ValueError` for invalid range/version). No other files changed besides this summary; tests untouched.
+
+**Verified:**
+- `python -m unittest`: 8 tests, all OK.
+- Ad-hoc script (not committed) checking about 30 cases taken from the doc tables/examples (partials, hyphen, tilde, caret zero cases, prerelease rule, `v` prefix, build metadata, `||` with empty set) and 7 invalid inputs (`1.x.3`, `>=`, `1.2.3 -`, `^`, etc.) raising `ValueError`: all as expected.
+
+**Unsure / assumptions:**
+- Doc conflict: "empty set / `*` matches every version" vs. the prerelease rule. I applied the prerelease rule, so `*` and `""` do not match prerelease versions such as `1.0.0-beta` (npm behaviour). Easy to change in `_in_set`.
+- `>*` / `<*` match nothing (npm behaviour; not in doc). `~>` is not supported.
+- No tests added for the extra cases.
